{
 "case": "N05-LINEAGE-NEG",
 "says": "On her laptop Alice commits a first and a second revision of her private notes source, the second expecting the head the first moved to. A third commit still expecting the first head is answered stale with stale_base and moves nothing; resealed on the current head it commits. Then two packages from her own authority arrive. The first names her authority's founding epoch and a successor that hands finalizing from the desktop to the laptop; it is staged and received, not accepted. The second names the same founding epoch and a different successor of it that hands finalizing to her phone. Accepting the second is refused with fork_evidence, and accepting the first after that is refused with fork_evidence too: two successors of one predecessor are fork evidence that no epoch number or arrival order resolves. What must not happen: the stale commit moving the head, or either successor becoming the authority's head — neither accept returns a receipt or an accepted or committed stage.",
